### Allsafe: Gideon, Angela, the servers.

=== gideon
-- start
? flag.da_price_gideon & !flag.gideon_framed & !flag.da_betrayed & !flag.gideon_warned_frame -> price_warn
? q.mq_hello>=35 & !q.mq_hello.done -> go_servers
? flag.knows_allsafe_ecorp & !flag.gideon_leverage_done & q.mq_hello.done -> know
? q.mq_rootkit.started -> later
? !q.mq_hello>=30 -> early
GIDEON: Elliot. Thank you for coming in. I mean that. E Corp's CTO has called me eleven times since midnight, and I have run out of new ways to say 'we're looking into it.'
* "Show me what you've got." -> trace
* [SPEECH 25] "Tell me the truth first. How bad is it for Allsafe if E Corp walks?" -> pressure | trace
* "What's CS30 doing open in the first place?" -> why_open
-- early
GIDEON: Elliot? What are you doing here? I said nine. In the morning. Go home. Talk to a human being. Sleep. The anomaly will still be anomalous tomorrow, I promise you.
-> END
-- why_open
GIDEON: It's a honeypot. You leave a door unlocked so you can watch who tries the handle. Except this one was opened wider than I approved. Someone changed the firewall rule last week. With my credentials. I didn't do it.
ELLIOT (V.O.): Gideon doesn't lie. He's bad at it. His ears go red. They're not red.
! set knows_cs30_widened
-> trace
-- pressure
GIDEON: Bad. E Corp is sixty percent of our revenue. If they walk, Allsafe is gone in a quarter. Everyone here. Angela. The new kids. Me. So when I ask for your eyes, I need them clean.
! set knows_allsafe_ecorp
-> trace
-- trace
GIDEON: The CS30 box is in the server room, at the back. Pull the logs, trace whoever knocked, write me something I can read to a man who owns a jet. And Elliot, whatever you find, you bring it to me first. Before E Corp. Before anyone.
! quest mq_hello 35 ; fame allsafe 2
-> END
-- price_warn
GIDEON: Elliot. You look like you're about to tell me someone died. Did someone die?
ELLIOT (V.O.): Not yet. I could still make it so nobody does. I could also just log in at his desk and go home.
* "Gideon. Someone is going to try to make it look like you're fsociety's insider. Lock everything. Get a lawyer. Today." -> warn_frame
* "No. Nothing. Forget it." -> END
-- warn_frame
> Gideon goes very still. Then he closes his office door, very quietly, and sits down.
GIDEON: ...Thank you. I'm not going to ask how you know. I'm going to call my lawyer, and my husband, and then I'm going to be very, very boring for a while.
ELLIOT (V.O.): Whiterose will know by morning. She keeps every clock. I just made an enemy of a woman who doesn't have to hurry.
! set gideon_warned_frame ; set da_betrayed ; hostile_faction darkarmy ; quest mq_darkarmy 40 ; quest mq_darkarmy done ; trust gideon 3 ; stab 6 ; xp 80
-> END
-- go_servers
GIDEON: Server room. Back of the office. CS30. Go on, I'll be here, practicing my apologetic face.
-> END
-- know
! set gideon_leverage_done
GIDEON: You've been in the contract files. I can tell. You know what E Corp is to this company. To all of us.
ELLIOT (V.O.): One client. Fifty jobs. Gideon's whole life, balanced on the goodwill of the thing I want to destroy. If I burn E Corp, I burn him too.
* "Your company's clean, Gideon. Whatever happens, that's on them." -> clean
* [SPEECH 40] "You should get out. Sell Allsafe while it's worth something." -> warn | clean
-- clean
GIDEON: I hope you're right. I've spent ten years being right about machines and wrong about people. Don't be the thing that proves the pattern.
-> END
-- warn
GIDEON: ...You know something. I've known you long enough to hear it. I won't ask. But Elliot, if this ship goes down, get yourself off it first. Promise me that much.
! set gideon_warned ; fame allsafe 3
-> END
-- later
? flag.gideon_framed -> later_framed
? q.mq_rootkit>=40 -> later_done
? flag.dat_reported -> later_reported
GIDEON: Anything on the coffee shop? Ron's, a few blocks from your place. It's always the small ones. Go look before E Corp's people do.
-> END
-- later_reported
GIDEON: I sent the file you found to E Corp's security team and the FBI liaison, like you said. Someone from the Bureau already called me back. A woman. She asked about you, actually. By name. I said you were the best I had. I hope that was the right answer.
-> END
-- later_done
GIDEON: The coffee shop server went quiet. Whatever was knocking on E Corp's door stopped. I'd call that a win if my stomach agreed. You look like someone who knows more than he's saying. You always do.
-> END
-- later_framed
> Gideon's office is half-packed. There's a box on his chair with a plant in it. His hands are shaking.
GIDEON: They think it was me. The FBI. They found my credentials on the fsociety servers, my name in the logs, a bank account in Cyprus I have never heard of. I've worked for twenty years to build something honest, Elliot. Twenty years.
ELLIOT (V.O.): I did this. Or I let it be done. In the Rose Garden it felt like arithmetic. Here it's a man packing a plant into a box.
-> END

=== angela
-- start
? item.colby_archive>=1 & !flag.township_resolved -> colby
? flag.knows_angela_plan -> plan
? flag.angela_ecorp -> ecorp
ANGELA: Elliot! You look like you slept in a server rack. Again. Allsafe's whole future is E Corp, and E Corp's having a bad night, so today matters. Are you with me?
* "I'm with you. I'm always with you." -> warm ! trust angela 1
* "Focus. E Corp logs first, feelings never." -> cold
* [SPEECH 30] "Angela. Why do you really work here? It's not the money." -> probe | cold
-- warm
ANGELA: You fixed my laptop once with a forum post and pure spite. Never change. Okay — change a little. Sleep.
-> hook
-- cold
ANGELA: You always do this. Go cold right when it's about to be real. Fine. Logs. Feelings later. There's always a later with you, and it never comes.
-> hook
-- probe
ANGELA: ...Because E Corp took something from me. From both of us, actually. Washington Township. You were there. You were a kid, but you were there.
! set knows_township_hint ; trust angela 1
ANGELA: I'm going to make them pay for it. I don't know how yet. But I will. Don't you dare tell me it's impossible.
-> hook
-- hook
ANGELA: Whatever it is you go off and do at night — I've got your back. Even when you go full ghost mode on me. Even then.
-> END
-- colby
ELLIOT (V.O.): I have it. Colby's emails from 1993. E Corp knew about the leak. They ran the numbers on our parents' lives and decided the settlement was cheaper than the cleanup. It's all here, in his own words.
ANGELA: Is that— Elliot. Is that what I think it is. After all these years. We could sue. We could put it in every paper. We could finally make them—
* "Give it to the lawyers. Do it right. It'll take years but it'll be real." -> colby_legal
* "Publish it. Tonight. Let everyone see what E Corp is." -> colby_leak
* "Keep it. It's leverage. Worth more held than spent." -> colby_hold
-- colby_legal
ANGELA: The right way. The slow way. Our parents waited twenty years — I guess we can wait a few more. Thank you. For finding it. For handing it to me instead of using it. That's not like you, and I love that it happened anyway.
! quest sq_colby done ; set township_resolved ; trust angela 3 ; fame locals 4 ; stab 5
-> END
-- colby_leak
ANGELA: Do it. Burn them with it. I don't want careful. I want the whole world to know their names by morning.
! quest sq_colby done ; set township_resolved ; set township_public ; infamy ecorp 5 ; fame fsociety 4 ; trust angela 2 ; stab 2
-> END
-- colby_hold
ANGELA: ...You're keeping it. Of course you are. Everything's a weapon to you, even our dead parents. I understand it. I hate that I understand it. Just— don't lose it. Please.
! quest sq_colby done ; set township_resolved ; set township_leverage ; trust angela -1
-> END
-- plan
ANGELA: You went through my laptop. Don't lie, you've got that look. So you know. I'm going to work for them. Inside. Where the levers are.
ELLIOT (V.O.): She wants to burn E Corp from the inside, one clean promotion at a time. I want to burn it from the outside, tonight. Same fire. Different fuse.
* "It'll change you before you change it. It always does." -> plan_warn
* "Then we're aiming at the same thing. Good." -> plan_ally ! trust angela 2 ; set angela_ally
* [SPEECH 45] "Don't. Come with me instead. There's a faster way." -> plan_recruit | plan_warn
-- plan_warn
ANGELA: Maybe. But at least I'll be in the room. You blow things up from a basement, Elliot. I want to be at the table. Somebody has to be.
-> END
-- plan_ally
ANGELA: Same thing. God. It's almost a relief to hear you say it. Don't blow me up by accident, okay? Warn me first.
-> END
-- plan_recruit
ANGELA: A faster way. There's always a faster way with you, and it always has a body count. No. I'll do it my way. But... keep the door open. In case my way fails.
! set angela_door_open
-> END
-- ecorp
ANGELA: I did it. I took the job at E Corp. Don't look at me like that. I'm exactly where I need to be. So are you, probably. We just picked different doors into the same building.
-> END

=== allsafe_servers
-- start
? q.mq_hello.done -> after
? !q.mq_hello>=35 -> idle
ELLIOT (V.O.): CS30. A box built to be broken into. Somebody took the invitation last night, at 3:40 in the morning.
> You pull the logs. The intrusion came in through a relay, bounced twice, and landed from a small server on the Lower East Side. A coffee shop. Ron's. Four blocks from your apartment.
ELLIOT (V.O.): That's not the part that makes my hands go cold. The payload. I know this payload. I read it last night, on my own desktop, at the end of a file called fsociety00.dat. It's byte for byte the same code.
ELLIOT (V.O.): Twenty-two missing minutes at 3:09. The honeypot hit at 3:40. Ron's is a ten minute walk from my apartment.
ELLIOT (V.O.): No. I was asleep. I'm almost sure I was asleep.
* Keep it. Tell Gideon the trace dead-ends at a coffee shop and nothing more. -> keep
* Report everything to Gideon: the payload, the file on your machine, all of it. -> report
* Wipe the payload from the logs and delete the file on your machine. Make it never have happened. -> wipe
-- keep
ELLIOT (V.O.): I write Gideon a clean report. Coffee shop, compromised server, recommend we have a look. Not a word about the file. If someone is using my hands, I want to find them before anyone else does.
! set dat_kept ; quest mq_hello done ; quest mq_rootkit 10 ; xp 50
-> END
-- report
ELLIOT (V.O.): I tell him everything. He listens without blinking, then he says the thing I knew he'd say: 'This goes to E Corp and the Bureau. Today.' He's right. That's the worst part of Gideon. He's usually right.
ELLIOT (V.O.): Whoever put that file on my machine is going to know I talked. Good. Let them come.
! set dat_reported ; quest mq_hello done ; quest mq_rootkit 10 ; fame allsafe 4 ; trust gideon 2 ; xp 50
-> END
-- wipe
ELLIOT (V.O.): Three commands. The payload is gone from the logs; my report says 'unknown origin, coffee shop relay.' At home, the file will be gone by the time I get there. I'll scrub the drive twice. I'll still be able to see it when I close my eyes.
! set dat_deleted ; quest mq_hello done ; quest mq_rootkit 10 ; stab -2 ; xp 50
-> END
-- idle
ELLIOT (V.O.): The server room hums. Honeypots, backups, a rack of machines that never sleep. Somebody else's problem until Gideon makes it mine.
-> END
-- after
ELLIOT (V.O.): CS30 still blinks in the dark. Somebody left a door open with Gideon's credentials. Somebody who knew which door I'd walk through.
-> END
